@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Creating and Managing Projects in Azure DevOps";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <h1 class="text-center text-primary">Creating and Managing Projects in Azure DevOps</h1>
    <p class="lead text-center">Learn how to create, configure, and efficiently manage projects in Azure DevOps.</p>
    <hr />

    <!-- Creating a Project -->
    <div class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="text-success">Creating a New Project</h2>
        <p>
            Azure DevOps allows you to create projects to manage and collaborate on software development tasks.
            Follow these steps to create a new project:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item">Navigate to <strong>Azure DevOps</strong> and sign in.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Click on <strong>New Project</strong> in the top-right corner.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Enter the project name, description, and choose visibility (Private/Public).</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Select a version control system (Git or TFVC) and a work item process (Agile, Scrum, etc.).</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Click <strong>Create</strong> to finalize your project setup.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/azure-devops-create-project.jpg" alt="Creating a Project in Azure DevOps" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Creating a new project in Azure DevOps.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Managing Projects -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-warning">Managing Your Projects</h2>
        <p>
            Once a project is created, you can manage it effectively using Azure DevOps tools:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Boards:</strong> Track work items, backlogs, and sprints.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Repos:</strong> Manage and collaborate on source code.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Pipelines:</strong> Automate builds, testing, and deployment.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Test Plans:</strong> Manage test cases and ensure software quality.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Artifacts:</strong> Share and manage package dependencies.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/azure-devops-manage-projects.jpg" alt="Managing Projects in Azure DevOps" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Managing a project with Azure DevOps tools.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Best Practices -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-info">Best Practices for Project Management</h2>
        <p>
            To maximize efficiency, follow these best practices:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item">Define clear goals and milestones for your project.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Use Agile or Scrum methodologies for better collaboration.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Automate testing and deployments using CI/CD pipelines.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Regularly review and update work items.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Ensure proper access control and security configurations.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/azure-devops-best-practices.jpg" alt="Best Practices for Managing Projects" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Effective project management strategies in Azure DevOps.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Conclusion -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-danger">Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Azure DevOps provides powerful tools for creating and managing projects efficiently. By following best practices and leveraging built-in features, teams can improve collaboration, automate workflows, and ensure project success.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/azure-devops-conclusion.jpg" alt="Conclusion on Managing Projects" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Enhance software development with Azure DevOps.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>